    "description": "Freddie Mac\n-Developed PMO Genie, a project portfolio management (PPM) web application with an extensible UI requirements that currently supports 2 enterprise programs across 20+ workstreams and scales to onboard future programs.\n-Streamlined complex data collection workflows by building intuitive forms and reusable dashboard components, cutting 12+ hours of manual team input weekly.\n-Integrated generative AI reporting capabilities on the client side to automate executive summary generation from centralized project data, cutting manual reporting turnaround times by 50%.\n\nJefferies\n-Developed @lemon-ui, an enterprise design system monorepo (Turborepo, pnpm workspaces) delivering atomic UI components, cross-format design tokens, and a dedicated Storybook documentation site backed by Vitest testing.\n-Built a custom MCP server using Node.js and Zod, enabling AI assistants to interface directly with component APIs and design tokens to streamline developer workflows.\n\nHuntington National Bank\n-Migrated legacy monolithic Angular workflows to a modern React micro-frontend architecture using Module Federation, enabling independent feature deployments and modular team ownership.\n-Engineered a client-side interoperability layer using custom event messaging and cross-framework state bridging, ensuring seamless data synchronization and zero visual disruption between Angular and embedded React applications.\n\nPrudential\n-Developed dynamic, responsive web interfaces for a customer-facing health assessment platform and an internal administrative dashboard used for real-time policyholder data review.\n-Built a schema-driven dynamic form engine in React, collaborating with backend teams to render complex, branching question workflows dynamically from API metadata without requiring code deployments.",
